      "n": "WrongAnswerAudio1"
    },
    {
      "s": "",
      "t": "A",
      "n": "Intro2Audio"
    },
    {
      "s": "In the Harry Potter books, Voldemort shattered his soul into pieces, hiding them away in everyday objects. They were called Horcruxes. And no part of Voldemort’s soul wound up in a knife.",
      "t": "A",
      "v": "734193_2",
      "n": "ExplanationAudio"
    },
    {
      "s": "Because even Voldemort knew the greatest magic of all is a power ballad sung by a Canadian with a mullet.",
      "t": "A",
      "v": "734194_3",
      "n": "JokeAudio"
    },
    {
      "s": "Imagine Harry Potter, on a nostalgia kick, makes a ‘Horcrux Shout-Out!’ Spotify playlist. Which song would Harry NOT include?",
